              {
                "id": "R1-001",
                "lens": "risk",
                "location": ".github/workflows/ci.yml:524-526",
                "severity": "WARNING",
                "claim": "The CI job runs staticcheck via 'go run honnef.co/go/tools/cmd/staticcheck@v0.7.0'. This fetches and executes third-party code at a version tag without checksum pinning beyond the Go module proxy and sum database. The same pattern is used by the identity job, so it is consistent with the repository. The code runs with read-only workflow permissions on checkout only, so no concrete exploit is reachable from this change.",
                "proof_refs": [
                  ".github/workflows/ci.yml:524-526"
                ],
                "causal_disposition": "introduced"
              }
            ],
            "evidence": [
              "I reviewed all 21 manifest paths. The change adds a new read-only Go module that uses only the standard library, so it adds no third-party dependency and no lockfile.",
              "The readers open files read-only. Only the fields needed for usage are decoded, and output holds aggregates only. The privacy sentinel test fixtures check that no content leaks to stdout.",
              "The log roots and price file path come from CLI flags that the local user chooses. There is no network input, no privilege boundary, no shell execution and no secret handling, so I found no reachable injection or exposure.",
              "Price parsing is strict: it rejects duplicate keys, unknown fields, trailing data, and NaN, Infinity or negative rates. This limits unsafe input handling.",
              "The only remark is the CI staticcheck invocation, reported as a WARNING because no concrete exploit follows from it."
            ]
          }
        }
