            "lens": "review-resilience",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "Reviewed all 21 manifest paths. The change is a new read-only CLI and library plus one new CI job, so no existing runtime behavior is altered.",
              "Failure handling in telemetry/readers.go degrades gracefully. Walk errors and unopenable files are counted in UnreadableFiles and the walk continues. Malformed lines are counted as Skipped. Lines are read with ReadBytes, so oversized lines do not abort the read. A missing or invalid agent meta file yields an empty agentType.",
              "In telemetry/cmd/telemetry/main.go, a missing default root is skipped with a note, while an explicit missing root exits 1. When nothing is readable it exits 1 with 'no readable source'. A bad price file exits 1 before any log is read.",
              "Memory is O(calls) for the retained context and cost slices and the per-file row map. The ledger records about 87k calls and about 9 s on the real corpus, so I found no concrete load or latency failure.",
              "Retry safety holds. Logs are only opened for reading, and the same input gives byte-identical output through sorted emission and canonical-order cost sums.",
              "I found no concrete production failure caused by this change and reachable with realistic input."
            ]
          }
        }
