            "findings": [
              {
                "id": "R3-001",
                "lens": "reliability",
                "location": "telemetry/readers.go:171-176",
                "severity": "WARNING",
                "claim": "A mid-file read error (non-EOF) increments UnreadableFiles, but the CLI treats a file as readable when Files \u003e UnreadableFiles. A failed walk entry (walkErr) increments UnreadableFiles without incrementing Files, which can skew that comparison. Partially read data is still emitted silently, and no test covers a mid-read I/O error.",
                "proof_refs": [
                  "telemetry/readers.go:171-176",
                  "telemetry/cmd/telemetry/main.go:73"
                ],
                "evidence_class": "inferential",
                "causal_disposition": "introduced"
              },
              {
                "id": "R3-002",
                "lens": "reliability",
                "location": "telemetry/readers.go:163-169",
                "severity": "WARNING",
                "claim": "For Pi, the first-seen-wins dedupe uses a root-wide seen map that is filled before the file's rows are emitted. Rows missing a usable ID are skipped, and a Pi line with no responseId and no id is dropped with no distinct counter. Duplicate-ID collisions between unrelated sessions that reuse fallback line IDs, such as small sequential IDs, would silently undercount calls. The tests use only the same ID in both files, so they do not show distinct sessions with colliding fallback IDs being kept.",
                "proof_refs": [
                  "telemetry/readers.go:163-169",
                  "telemetry/readers_test.go:178-186"
                ],
                "evidence_class": "inferential",
                "causal_disposition": "introduced"
              }
            ],
            "evidence": [
              "Reviewed all 21 manifest paths. The module is new and read-only, so there is no baseline regression surface.",
              "Failure paths are covered by observable assertions: malformed lines, 2 MB lines, missing roots, broken symlinks, bad meta files, price-table validation, CLI exit codes 0, 1 and 2, and ordering determinism with shuffled insertion.",
              "Golden output and fixture stats are consistent with the fixture data. Recorded costs are never re-estimated, and without --prices the estimated_ fields are omitted.",
              "No BLOCKER or CRITICAL finding: the two warnings concern edge cases outside the realistic fixtures and have bounded impact."
            ]
          }
        }
